  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -2913,6 +2913,23 @@ upon the conversation index and values inside the request packets.\n     }\n \n \n+2.2.6 Registering your dissector for conversation filtering\n+\n+In cases where protocols define a conversation, you can register them through\n+the UI menu of Wireshark by locating \"Analyze -> Conversation Filter\". This can\n+reduce the task of isolating sessions and viewing them to a single click. For users\n+that frequent a specific protocol in a conversation, this may save time and reduce errors.\n+\n+When you have a protocol to add to the UI, use the add_conversation_filter_protocol() function.\n+Using this built-in function will allow you to add your dissector to a conversation, providing\n+only the packets relevant to the specified protocol in a conversation.\n+\n+\n+Example using the \"example_protocol\" protocol:\n+    Use the add_conversation_filter_protocol() function with the conversation and your \"example_protocol\":\n+        add_conversation_filter_protocol(example_protocol)\n+\n+\n \n 2.3 Dynamic conversation dissector registration.\n \n",
